win32u, winewayland: maximize on a monitor that is not the primary on a mixed-DPI desktop

Found 2026-10-14 testing the KDE-primary patch on a nested KWin laid out like GitHub Neutron#20 but at mixed scales
(1440x2560 portrait at 175% = 168 dpi at the origin, 2560x1440 landscape at 200% = 192 dpi): Illustrator 2026
maximized on whichever monitor was not Wine's primary came out wrong -- portrait-width on the landscape monitor with
its configure rejected, or too tall with its menu bar above the screen (240+ rejected configures). The #20 follow-
output fix had only been verified at 100%/100%. Three causes:

1. win32u monitor_from_rect() (upstream Wine 11.10): for a per-monitor-aware caller (dpi 0, raw pixels, as on
   Windows) map_dpi_rect() leaves the rect raw, but it was then compared against the monitors at the SYSTEM dpi.
   With system dpi 192, the raw point (1440,581) -- the landscape monitor's origin -- came back as the portrait
   monitor, whose 192-dpi rect is (0,0)-(1646,2926). The follow-output check therefore saw "same monitor" and never
   moved the window. Now dpi 0 compares raw with raw (as get_monitor_from_rect(.., 0, MDT_RAW_DPI) elsewhere).
   Kill switch NEUTRON_MONITOR_RAW_LOOKUP=0.

2. winewayland follow-output converted the compositor's logical size with the scale of the monitor the window was
   LEAVING: 823x1463 for the 175% portrait output became 1646x2926 at 200%. The size, and the frame overhang that is
   carried over, are now converted at the output's own scale (mode width / logical width).
   Kill switch NEUTRON_FOLLOW_SCALE=0.

3. The maximized work-area measurement (workarea#1/#2) was ONE value for every output, applied to any output it
   plausibly fit; a panel-less output got a borrowed or 32px-estimated inset, the window came out 32 logical px short
   of the configure (823x1431 against 823x1463), the compositor rejected every commit, and Illustrator snapped back
   to the short work area each time. Measurements now carry the output they were taken on (reported from follow-
   output, which runs after every maximized configure and when a surface settles on one output) and are kept and
   persisted per output name; the single value is used only while no output has its own. The prefix file keeps the
   single value on its first line for older runtimes. Kill switch NEUTRON_WORKAREA_PER_OUTPUT=0.

Also: a NEUTRON_WL_DIAG trace of the follow-output decision (probe and window monitors with their rects).

Verified on the nested KWin, clean-room Illustrator 2026, runtime 11.10-123 + the maximized-crop and KDE-primary
patches, LogPixels 192 (what the CLI sets for a 200% KDE primary):
- landscape not primary (old rule): before -> portrait-width, configure rejected; with 1 -> moved, one rejection;
  with 1+2 -> moved straight to (1440,581)-(4000,2021), no rejection; full size with its menu bar.
- portrait not primary (KDE primary = landscape): before -> 1646x2926 placed, menu bar above the screen; with
  1+2+3 -> moved to the portrait monitor at its own size.
- every case clean (no rejection, menu bar visible) once the output has a measurement; the first maximize ever on
  an output whose real work area differs from the 32px estimate can still come out misplaced in that session.
- operator's desk (4K 175% with a top panel, second output at (2195,94)): the 4K unchanged, (-5,51)-(3845,2165),
  no sliver; the prefix file gains "Virtual-0 1202" / "Virtual-1 1080".

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -4793,12 +4793,36 @@
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON: kill switch for the raw-coordinate lookup in monitor_from_rect (NEUTRON_MONITOR_RAW_LOOKUP=0). */
+static BOOL neutron_monitor_raw_lookup(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (v < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_MONITOR_RAW_LOOKUP" ); v = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return v;
+}
+
 static HMONITOR monitor_from_rect( const RECT *rect, UINT flags, UINT dpi )
 {
     struct monitor *monitor;
     HMONITOR ret = 0;
     RECT r;
 
+    /* NEUTRON: dpi 0 is a per-monitor-aware caller, whose coordinates are raw (physical) pixels, as on Windows.
+     * map_dpi_rect() leaves them raw, but they were then compared against the monitors at the SYSTEM dpi, which
+     * is a different space for every monitor whose dpi differs from it. Measured 2026-10-14 (nested KWin, a
+     * 1440x2560 portrait monitor at 168 dpi beside a 2560x1440 landscape one at (1440,581), system dpi 192): the
+     * raw point (1440,581) came back as the portrait monitor, whose 192-dpi rect is (0,0)-(1646,2926), so a
+     * maximized window the compositor showed on the landscape output was never moved there and kept a portrait
+     * size. Compare raw with raw. */
+    if (!dpi && neutron_monitor_raw_lookup())
+    {
+        if (!lock_display_devices( FALSE )) return 0;
+        if ((monitor = get_monitor_from_rect( *rect, flags, 0, MDT_RAW_DPI ))) ret = monitor->handle;
+        unlock_display_devices();
+        TRACE( "%s flags %x raw returning %p\n", wine_dbgstr_rect(rect), flags, ret );
+        return ret;
+    }
+
     r = map_dpi_rect( *rect, dpi, system_dpi );
 
     if (!lock_display_devices( FALSE )) return 0;
